<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 21 April, from 753 BCE to 1960.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">753 BCE</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Romulus founds Rome, according to Roman tradition</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Roman writers placed the city's foundation by Romulus on the Palatine on 21 April 753 BCE, a date fixed by the scholar Varro. Romans celebrated it each year as the Parilia.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1506</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Three days of massacre in Lisbon come to an end</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rioting stirred up by Dominican friars killed between 1,000 and 4,000 New Christians, Jews forcibly converted in 1497. King Manuel I punished the city and had two of the friars executed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-christians">New Christians</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1782</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rama I founds Bangkok as Siam's new capital</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The city pillar of Bangkok was erected on the east bank of the Chao Phraya, marking the official founding of the new royal capital. It replaced Thonburi across the river.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1836</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Texans defeat Santa Anna at San Jacinto</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sam Houston's army surprised the Mexican camp and won in about eighteen minutes. Santa Anna was captured the next day and forced to order his troops out of Texas, securing its independence.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1918</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Red Baron is shot down and killed near Amiens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Manfred von Richthofen, credited with 80 victories, was killed while pursuing an enemy aircraft over the Somme. Whether a Canadian pilot or Australian ground gunners fired the fatal shot is still debated.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1960</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Brasília is inaugurated as Brazil's capital</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Built in under four years to plans by Lúcio Costa and Oscar Niemeyer, Brasília replaced Rio de Janeiro as capital. It was meant to draw development into Brazil's interior.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></li></ol>
